{"kind":"report","text":"Checker review of S1's plan-only recovery at head eece533e9e7c98662c09eea5231a4a41ffc9a8e1, tree 5f36bb41, for child request 84aec6ab and review request a2049e19. Verdict: APPROVED for the seven reviewed paths only.\n\n**This verdict does not approve a landing of this head.** The branch changes 53 paths from main, and I reviewed seven. `gs merge` checks which artifacts a landing retires, not whether every path in the commit was reviewed, so the tool may not stop a merge of this commit. Do not merge on this approval. Whole-S1 review at a later exact head comes first, after the scratch witnesses, as request 84aec6ab and promise 0fdaaca9 state. This verdict permits the same approved scratch B operation to continue under ruling ee25224c.\n\nI read the implementation note first, then the five recovery files and the manifest. The diff from cc2892f4 to the gated source changes only `identities.ts`, `diagnostics.ts`, `setup.ts`, `runbook.md` and `test/identities.test.ts`.\n\n## Against ruling ee25224c\n\n1. Same plan, operation, home, actor and inputs. Resolved.\n   - `enrollment` compares the retained plan with the plan rebuilt from the owner's current state, field by field and by digest (`identities.ts:352-355`). `planOnly` compares the retained global SetupPlan and checks the digest again.\n   - The receiver must be the fixed home for that handle and kind.\n2. Empty custody. Resolved. The receiver may hold only its plan file: no issue pointer, handoff, STARTED marker, configuration, key or enrollment original. The owner may hold no invitation pointer. Each case has its own refusal test.\n3. Any orphan or conflict stops. Resolved.\n   - An owner `i-` file counts only through another fixed receiver's completed phase marker, exact plan and handoff, a hash-checked chain, and leaf bindings for operation, actor, service, repository, input, secret and receipts.\n   - A file that nothing owns stops the run, with `plan-only-orphan`, even when it names this operation. The test covers a matching and a foreign orphan.\n4. Only the first root, durable before any act. Resolved.\n   - Continue calls the maintained engine in new mode. `keepPrivate` repeats the whole proof before the first root, checks each row's operation, actor, service, repository and input, and writes the pointer and the original before dispatch.\n   - The test reads the retained original at the moment of dispatch and compares it with the signed act.\n   - The wrong-actor control removes `row[\"actor\"] !== plan.actor`. Its baseline passes 6 of 6, and its mutant fails only that assertion on an ordinary `AssertionError`, with the source restored.\n5. Check stays read-only. Resolved. It refuses `original-invitation-missing` before the proof runs, and the test shows the receiver's private directory unchanged.\n6. Nothing retained is remade. Resolved. The branch creates no replacement signature, key, secret, deadline or room. A missing original still stops.\n7. The pre-root exit status and stderr. Resolved, with point 1 below.\n   - Each invocation needs a new owner-only directory outside the private homes. The helper flushes and reads back its exit code and its fixed stderr line before it exits.\n   - The projection holds fixed stages, whitelisted reasons, and the read's method, category and status. No body, header, key, link or exception message can reach it, and the test checks that with secret-bearing errors.\n   - The note says that the initial B cause stays unknown, and it infers none.\n\nBounds hold as stated: 512 leaves per directory, 16 originals per chain, and 64 KiB decoded with an 87,385-byte file ceiling per original. `boundPrivate` checks shape, links, owner, mode and size before the inherited reader allocates, and unique metadata reads share one 4 MiB ceiling. The note says that these local samples are no atomic snapshot and no native authority. That qualification is right.\n\n## The gate\n\n- The gate at b221af60, tree 3d872ea1, passes all five stages. Receipt 77937e2c exits 0 with complete capture, the same head and tree before and after, and no dropped bytes. Node passes 86 cases, Counting 56, Plain 3,162 with one skip and Native 859 with two skips.\n- From b221af60 to the head, only the note and the manifest change, which the documents-only rule in `docs/testing.md` covers.\n- Earlier failures stay recorded in the note: gates 1 and 2, the compiler failure and the first scratch stops.\n\n## Checks at this head\n\n- The worktree is clean. `git merge-tree --write-tree` onto main 5dc9765f gives the head tree 5f36bb41.\n- The seven artifacts are all at this head, with the note first and filed last, so the commitment's report is the note. Each reads stale only because it rests on a question the builder retired after reading its ruling.\n- I ran `examples/repo-in-ai/test/identities.test.ts` once: 6 of 6. The builder worktree stayed clean.\n- The evidence verifies. The manifest has SHA-256 3f1f9e83. All 189 cited files match by size and SHA-256. The directory has 614 files and 66,338,423 bytes, its `SHA256SUMS` has digest 747d88c4 and reruns clean, and no file is unlisted or writable.\n- check-doc-links on an export of the head: 764 links, 0 broken.\n- check-notes from 5dc9765f: 0 warnings.\n- check-commit-messages from 5dc9765f: 10 checked, 0 flagged.\n- `git diff --check`: clean.\n\n## Points that do not block\n\n1. A recurrence may still be hard to diagnose. An exception with no recognized code or read status records only `engine-error`, and a failure before enrollment starts, such as in `checkDeployment` or `session`, records `enrollment: null`. A fixed list of error class names would add information safely, and so would a stage for the deployment check. The ruling asks for a diagnosable recurrence, so this is worth doing if B stops again.\n2. No test tampers with a completed peer's proof (`plan-only-prior-proof`), and no test places a symbolic link in the custody paths. Both refusals exist in the code.\n3. A crash after the receiver pointer is written and before the owner original is written leaves `private-original-missing` on the next run. That stop is safe under the ruling, but it ends this identity's recovery.\n4. If `diagnostics.finish` fails after a successful phase, the helper exits 1 for work that completed. The phase marker is already kept, so the next Check settles it.\n5. The note still uses \"Root\" for the builder.\n\n## Architecture\n\nThe recovery stays in the example's helper, over the maintained CLI engine, and adds no kernel, platform or room rule. Approved for the seven paths.\n\n## Security\n\nThe branch can start only one first root, and only after two complete custody proofs. Each row is bound to its actor and inputs, and the public diagnostics can't carry a private value. The proofs establish local custody and grant no native authority, as the note says. Approved for the seven paths.\n\n## Simplification\n\nOne branch handles one proven state, and every other state stops. The proof is long because each ownership link needs its own check, and I see no safe shorter form. Approved.\n\n## Conclusions\n\n- Architecture: approved for the seven paths.\n- Security: approved for the seven paths.\n- Simplification: approved.\n- The request's checks: same-plan proof, first-root admission, retained-original refusal, pre-root diagnostics, the actual-engine owner and control, the passing gate with a documents-only tail, and the evidence all hold.\n- Still open: the repaired B Continue, the seed comparison, the review-permission witness, credential release, the real room, and exact whole-S1 review before any landing. This verdict claims none of them.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:e7e0fe697f2085862a89f875c18cbbefea514bc6","binding":"assigned","head":"eece533e9e7c98662c09eea5231a4a41ffc9a8e1","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:b6ec091ef8408921fd940956e7f33